<p>Seattle is expensive, but it also pays. Household incomes are among the highest in the country, Washington has no personal income tax, and the city's tech workers would much rather pay someone than spend a rare sunny Saturday scraping moss off the roof. That makes the best side hustles in Seattle a mix of high-skill freelance work and practical services that busy people gladly outsource.</p>
<p>Below are 18 side gigs in Seattle that work in 2026, with typical pay, startup cost and the local details that help you stand out. We also cover the part most guides skip: Washington's business license, B&amp;O tax and Seattle's own license requirements.</p>

