<h2 id="seattle-advantage">The Seattle advantage (and the catch)</h2>
<p>The advantage is demand. Amazon, Microsoft, Boeing, Starbucks, Nordstrom, the University of Washington, Fred Hutch and dozens of startups in South Lake Union and Bellevue employ hundreds of thousands of well-paid people. They need skills, and they need time.</p>
<p>The catch is cost. Rent, parking and car ownership are expensive, so low-margin gigs barely cover themselves. Favor side jobs in Seattle that use a skill, a bike or a tool you already own, and price for the local market rather than national averages.</p>
<p>Seattle's calendar matters too. Cruise season runs roughly April through October out of Pier 66 and Pier 91, summer brings Seafair and long dry days, and fall through spring is the rainy season when moss, leaves and clogged gutters keep home-service crews busy.</p>

