<p>Washington sets minimum per-mile and per-minute earnings for rideshare drivers, and Seattle's App-Based Worker Minimum Payment ordinance sets a pay floor for delivery work done in the city. That doesn't guarantee profit, but it makes app work more predictable than in most states.</p>
