<h2 id="get-started">How to start a side hustle in Seattle this month</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Pick a gig that matches the season.</strong> Fall and winter favor gutters, lights and delivery; spring and summer favor pressure washing, boats, events and pet sitting.</li>
  <li><strong>Check your day-job contract.</strong> Many tech employers have moonlighting rules. Know them before you take a client.</li>
  <li><strong>Register your business.</strong> Get a Washington business license and a Seattle business license tax certificate if they apply to you.</li>
  <li><strong>Set prices for Seattle, not the national average.</strong> Use our <a href="/tools/freelance-rate-calculator/">freelance rate calculator</a> to account for costs and platform fees.</li>
  <li><strong>Get three reviews, then raise your rates.</strong> Nextdoor and neighborhood groups move quickly on recommendations.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="washington-taxes">Washington taxes, B&amp;O and Seattle licensing</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>No state income tax:</strong> Washington doesn't tax personal income, so your side profit only faces federal income tax and 15.3% self-employment tax. Estimate it with our <a href="/tools/self-employment-tax-calculator/">self-employment tax calculator</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>State business license:</strong> required once you meet triggers such as the state's annual gross income threshold, collecting sales tax or using a trade name.</li>
  <li><strong>State B&amp;O tax:</strong> Washington taxes gross receipts, not profit. Small businesses get a credit that often wipes out the tax, but filing requirements still apply depending on your assigned frequency.</li>
  <li><strong>Seattle license and B&amp;O:</strong> most businesses operating in Seattle need a business license tax certificate. From January 1, 2026, the city's B&amp;O threshold rose to $2 million in taxable revenue, so side hustles rarely owe city B&amp;O, but you must still renew the license, pay the license fee and file returns.</li>
  <li><strong>Sales tax on some services:</strong> Washington treats some services, such as certain landscaping work, as retail sales. Check with the Department of Revenue before you assume a service is exempt.</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Watch out:</strong> Short-term rental hosts in Seattle need a city short-term rental license and are limited in how many units they can operate. If you co-host, confirm the owner is licensed before you take bookings.</div>

